      "source": "wiktionary",
      "url": "https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/march",
      "quote": "{{dercat|en|ine-pro}} From {{inh|en|enm|marchen}}, from {{der|en|frm|marcher|t=to march, walk}}, from {{der|en|fro|marchier|t=to stride, to march, to trample}}, from {{der|en|frk|*markōn|t=to mark, mark out, to press with the foot}}, from {{der|en|gem-pro|*markōną|t=to mark}}. Akin to {{cog|ang|mearc}}, {{m|ang|ġemearc|t=mark, boundary}}. Compare {{m|en|mark}}, from {{inh|en|ang|mearcian}}. Compare typologically {{m+|ru|сле́довать}} (akin to {{m|ru|след}}). Also compare {{m|ru|пятно́}} (<~ {{m|ru|пята́}})."
    },
    {
      "source": "etymonline",
      "url": "https://www.etymonline.com/word/march",
      "quote": "\"to walk with measured steps or a regular tread,\" either individually or as a body, early… See origin and meaning of march. from Old French marcher \"to stride, march, walk,\" originally \"to trample, tread underfoot,\" a word of uncertain origin."
